Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Fri Nov 20 01:56:40 2026 +0300

    fix(ui): make PacedTerminalWriter pace output that arrives one chunk a turn
    
    The budget was per drain pass, and a pass ended as soon as the queue was
    empty. A PTY stream delivers one chunk per event-loop turn, so every pass
    wrote its single chunk and returned: the budget was never reached and no
    frame was ever waited for. Through a real PTY the writer changed nothing -
    one frame in a 2-3 s burst, with or without it.
    
    The budget is now per frame, summed across write() calls. Once it is spent,
    output is queued until a frame has been produced. A chunk arriving after a
    frame interval of idleness starts a fresh budget and is written at once, so
    ordinary output is not delayed. If no frame comes within 100ms the writer
    stops waiting for it and leaves one frame interval between budgets instead,
    so a hidden window still drains.
    
    Example app, real PTY, 64 MiB, 100x37, longest gap between frames:
    ascii 318 -> 19 ms, mixed unicode 2321 -> 48 ms, CJK 2847 -> 23 ms, at
    8-21% lower throughput. Public API unchanged.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

