Date:   Wed Nov 11 00:16:35 2026 +0300

    fix(buffer): reflow cursor, wrapped-line erase, hidden cells, scrollback
    
    - Reflow keeps the cursor in place when a line exactly fills the new
      width; the next character no longer overwrites the last one, and a
      narrowing reflow no longer pushes the cursor's row into scrollback
      while blank rows remain below it.
    - ESC[K no longer clears the soft-wrap flag unless the whole row is
      erased, so copied text and reflow keep long lines joined.
    - Erased or reflowed text no longer reappears after shrinking and then
      widening the terminal.
    - getText emits a space for blank cells inside a row, so copying from
      TUIs keeps the gaps between words.
    - Lines scrolled out of a scroll region that starts at the top of the
      main screen are kept in scrollback.
    - Block selections dragged from top-right to bottom-left produce
      segments.
    - The saved cursor follows the screen when the height shrinks.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

