    fix(render): mouse rows with scrollback and scroll following
    
    - Mouse reports (including SGR pixel mode) no longer land one row too
      low once there is scrollback and the view height is not a multiple of
      the cell height; a scrolled-up view reports the screen row of the line
      actually clicked.
    - Scrolling back to the bottom while output is streaming resumes
      following new output.
    - With a full scrollback, a scrolled-up view keeps the same text in place
      as output arrives, until it is trimmed.
    - TerminalTheme has value equality, so rebuilding an equal theme no
      longer flushes the render caches or sends a colour-scheme report.
    
