Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 00:10:49 2026 +0300

    fix(parser): harden the escape parser against hostile output
    
    - Cap CSI numeric parameters at 65535. Huge values overflowed int64, threw
      a RangeError out of write() and dropped the rest of the chunk, and huge
      REP counts stalled the terminal.
    - Discard unrecognised ESC sequences with intermediate bytes (ESC % G,
      ESC SP F, ESC $ ( D) instead of printing their final byte.
    - Parse colon-form truecolor SGR without a colour-space field
      (38:2:R:G:B) correctly when more parameters follow.
    - An OSC whose terminator arrives exactly at the 8 KiB limit no longer
      swallows the terminator and all following output.
    - XTVERSION and DA2 report the current package version, with a test that
      reads pubspec.yaml so the constant cannot drift again.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

