Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Thu Oct 1 23:59:58 2026 +0300

    fix(input): let macOS input methods compose
    
    Typing 한글테스트 with the macOS 2-Set Korean input method sent the bare
    compatibility jamo ㅎㅏㄴㄱㅡㄹㅌㅔㅅㅡㅌㅡ to the PTY (SoFluffyOS/lumide#64).
    
    The text fallback in the key handler inserted every printable key and
    reported it handled, and the macOS embedder hands a key to the platform
    input method only when the framework leaves it unhandled. Printable key
    downs are now left to the input method while an input connection is
    attached.
    
    On a real Mac the Korean input method turned out not to use marked text:
    it rewrites the last character of the editing value in place and reads
    the previous character from it. The editing value is therefore no longer
    cleared while it ends in Hangul or from inside an editing update, what was
    sent is tracked by content, and a trailing Hangul character is held as the
    composing preview until something follows it, a key the terminal handles
    itself, a paste, focus loss, closing the keyboard or dispose.
    
    Linux, Windows, mobile, web and deleteDetection keep their previous
    behaviour; Linux does not serialize key events and needs a device to
    verify.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

