Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 21:50:33 2026 +0300

    fix(selection): keep a drag's start where it was pressed while scrolling
    
    The gesture handler kept the press as its pixel offset in the viewport and
    resolved it to a cell again on every update, against whatever the scroll
    offset was by then. Scrolling while the button was held, with the wheel or
    through the edge auto-scroller, moved the start of the selection by as many
    lines as the view had moved, so text longer than one screen could not be
    selected. Long-press selection on touch had the same flaw.
    
    The start is now a `CellAnchor` taken when the drag or long press begins,
    so it names the same cell however far the view scrolls, and also when a
    full scrollback drops lines off the top while the drag is held. The anchor
    is released when the gesture ends; `onLongPressUp` is wired up for that.
    
    The auto-scroll test only checked that the view scrolled and that some
    selection existed. It now checks where the selection starts, alongside new
    tests for a wheel scroll during a drag, scrollback trimmed during a drag,
    and a scroll during a long press. All four failed before this change.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

