    docs: resolve dartdoc reference and canonicalization warnings
    
    Seven doc comments wrote literals as `[true]`, `[false]`, `[null]` and two
    parameter names in square brackets, which dartdoc reads as symbol links and
    could not resolve. They become code spans.
    
    The barrels re-export the same symbols through more than one library, so
    dartdoc was picking a canonical home for each of them at 0.001 confidence.
    Give the barrels library directives and declare xterm canonical for the
    affected types, which is what dartdoc was already guessing.
    
    Four warnings remain, for the ambiguous library names themselves rather than
    symbols within them. {@canonicalFor} validates its target against classes,
    enums, mixins, functions, properties and typedefs, so a library name is
    structurally rejected and trades one warning for another.
    
    Also corrects the wording of deleteDetection's comment.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
