Date:   Sat Aug 29 11:03:05 2026 +0300

    fix: bound the rejected ligature run set
    
    _rejectedLigatureRuns exists so that runs which do not shape into a
    grid-aligned ligature stop competing for slots in _paragraphCache, but it had
    no bound of its own and was cleared only when the font or colours changed.
    Ordinary content saturates it at a few dozen entries; a stream of varied ASCII
    punctuation grows it for the lifetime of the painter.
    
    Cap it and clear it wholesale on overflow. Eviction is never a correctness
    problem here: a dropped rejection costs exactly the one re-layout the entry was
    there to avoid, so a per-key LRU would buy nothing over a plain clear.
    
    The accompanying test drives 700 distinct runs through the rejection path and
    fails at 700 entries when the cap is removed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GhpXeitADp8YvvtxFhMuPM

