Date:   Sat Aug 29 01:29:25 2026 +0300

    perf: take the surrogate decode off the per-code-point path
    
    `ByteConsumer.consume()` called `_decodeCodePoint` and
    `_codePointCodeUnitLength` on every code point, and each of them re-ran the
    same high-surrogate test to arrive at the same answer: a unit that does not
    start a surrogate pair is one code unit long and is its own code point.
    Testing once up front and returning covers everything outside astral text -
    CSI parameters, C0 controls, Latin, Cyrillic, and the per-code-point path
    for text the run scan could not batch.
    
    Equivalent by construction: both helpers return `first` and `1` on exactly
    the branch this takes, and rollback is unaffected because
    `_previousRuneOffset` already steps back one unit for a non-surrogate.
    
    Interleaved A/B, three rounds each, medians in MiB/s:
    
    | workload | full | parser |
