Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Thu Aug 6 21:50:03 2026 +0300

    fix(ui): snap rounded box corners onto the pixel grid
    
    Straight box-drawing arms go through fillBar, which rounds the bar's
    thickness and snaps its near edge onto the pixel grid with antialiasing
    off. The rounded corners bypassed that: they stroke a path centred on the
    raw cell centre with antialiasing on. At the fractional cell sizes real
    font metrics produce, that centre lands half a pixel off the grid, so the
    corner's tails antialias one pixel wider than the arms they continue into
    and step sideways where the two meet - a visible notch and a heavier
    stroke at every box corner.
    
