Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Thu Aug 6 00:45:46 2026 +0300

    feat(ui): add PacedTerminalWriter for smooth output bursts
    
    `flood` reports 37 frames per second while draining 32 MiB on a 170x50 grid.
    The reason is not a slow frame - the worst UI frame during the burst is 3.2ms -
    it is that parsing owns the thread between frames: the burst spends about 89%
    of its time in `Terminal.write` and 11% painting.
    
    `PacedTerminalWriter` queues output and parses it until a budget is spent, then
    yields so a frame can happen. Measured with the harness, which now runs the
    paced case alongside the unpaced one:
    
      unpaced      566ms   37.1 fps   worst UI frame 3.2ms
      paced, 8ms   854ms   74.9 fps   worst UI frame 1.9ms
      paced, 4ms  1068ms   74.9 fps   worst UI frame 1.4ms
    
    Twice the frames at the display's full refresh rate, for about 50% more drain
    time. 4ms buys nothing over 8ms, which is why 8ms is the default and the doc
    comment says to treat the budget as a stutter ceiling rather than a tuning
    knob.
    
    Opt-in, and nothing in the package uses it: which side of that trade an
    application wants is not this package's decision to make.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

