    refactor(terminal): extract reports, paste and context signals
    
    Continues the god-class split. Terminal drops from 3997 to 3210 lines by
    moving five self-contained concerns into part files:
    
    - terminal_terminfo.dart: the XTGETTCAP capability table, as library-level
      functions. The table is a constant; the only terminal state it depended on
      was the viewport size, now threaded through as columns/rows parameters.
    - terminal_status_string.dart: DECRQSS reply formatting, as a mixin. Its
      seven abstract members are the honest dependency footprint of reporting.
    - terminal_paste.dart: paste sanitization, as library-level functions. They
      are pure string transforms; Terminal.isPasteSafe stays as the public entry.
    - terminal_context_signal.dart: the OSC 3008 types and decoder.
    - terminal_device_settings.dart: fifteen settings written by an escape
      sequence and read back only by DECRQSS - the volumes, DECSLCK, DECSCL,
      the title modes, the DECATC colour table. This is the only move that
      carries state rather than code; Terminal keeps one-line delegating
      setters, and the clamping behaviour is preserved exactly.
    
    No public API change: the moved types stay in the same library, and
    Terminal's surface is unchanged.
    
    Note for future work: this repo is formatted with the older dart_style.
    Running the installed `dart format` rewrites terminal.dart wholesale into
    tall style, so it was not used here - the diff is content-only.
    
    Verified: dart analyze lib test example clean, 799 tests pass with the one
    pre-existing IME skip, XTERM2_FUZZ_ROUNDS=5000 green.
    
