    refactor(terminal): extract SGR attribute/color handlers into a mixin
    
    Second cut at the EscapeHandler method bodies, the largest remaining
    mass in terminal.dart. Unlike the semantic-prompt state (its own bundle
    of fields + logic), these ~50 methods are literally EscapeHandler
    overrides: they must stay members of the class that `implements
    EscapeHandler` for the interface to be satisfied, so they can't become a
    freestanding class the way `_TerminalModes` or `_SemanticPromptTracker`
    did. A mixin is the shape that fits: `_SgrHandlers` declares the three
    members it needs (`_cursorStyle`, `_assignedColors`, `_namedColor`) as
    abstract, Terminal's own same-named field/field/method satisfy them
    structurally (Dart checks this by shape, not declaration site), and
    `class Terminal with Observable, _SgrHandlers implements ...` picks the
    methods up as its own overrides. No `on Terminal` clause is needed or
    possible here (that would require Terminal to already extend the mixin's
    constraint before applying it, which is circular); declaring the three
    dependencies abstract sidesteps that entirely.
    
    Practical fallout: the annotate_overrides lint now asks for @override on
    _cursorStyle/_assignedColors/_namedColor in terminal.dart, since they
    satisfy the mixin's abstract members - added. The mixin's own methods
    drop @override (a mixin with no supertype/on-clause has nothing to
    override from its own point of view); the interface conformance is
    re-checked at the "class Terminal ... implements EscapeHandler" site
    either way, so nothing is unchecked.
    
    No behavior change: every method body is an unmodified move.
    terminal.dart: 4203 -> 3997 lines. New file: 192 lines.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

