Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 23:41:24 2026 +0300

    refactor(terminal): extract the OSC 133/633 semantic-prompt state machine
    
    Phase 2 of decomposing the Terminal god class. Continues phase 1's `part
    of` split rather than moving to separate libraries with explicit
    interfaces: part files share one library, so the compiler provably
    cannot let the public API drift as pieces move around, and every
    extraction so far has been driven by physically relocating code rather
    than redesigning it. Separate libraries would force real interfaces at
    every boundary; for a class this entangled with buffer/cursor internals,
    that pressure would either balloon those interfaces (passing _mainBuffer
    and _cursorStyle through) or force awkward call-backs, exactly the trap
    phase 1's agent hit and stopped at. `part of` keeps the risk to "did I
    move this code correctly," which is what the 799-test suite is built to
    catch.
    
    That correctly-scoped extraction is what unblocks this target. Phase 1
    stopped here because obviously bundling "semantic prompt state" also
    pulled in anchor lifecycle calls into `_mainBuffer` and the `_cursorStyle`
    writes those calls gate. The buffer coupling doesn't go away by choosing
    `part of` over separate libraries, but it also stops mattering: nothing
    requires the new class to own the buffer-touching parts just because it
    owns the state. `_SemanticPromptTracker` owns exactly the pure state
    machine: the current `TerminalSemanticPromptState`, the
    input-terminates-at-line-feed flag, the primary-prompt predicate, and the
    cursor-attribute mapping. Anchor bookkeeping
    (_recordSemanticPromptAnchor, _pruneSemanticPromptAnchors,
    _isValidSemanticPromptAnchor, _activeSemanticPromptOffset,
    _restoreActiveSemanticPrompt, _clearSemanticPromptAnchors) and the OSC
    133/633 dispatch methods that call into both stay on Terminal, since they
    already reach into _mainBuffer/_cursorStyle/onSemanticPrompt and gain
    nothing from being moved.
    
    No behavior change: TerminalSemanticPromptState, the four semantic-prompt
    enums, and the parsing helpers move file location only. terminal.dart:
    4401 -> 4203 lines. New file: 239 lines.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

