    Move the iTerm2 clipboard-capture state (selector, in-progress buffer,
    overflow flag) and its start/end/capture-char/capture-text-range logic
    out of Terminal into a new _ClipboardCapture class. Unlike the two
    prior extractions this one moves behavior, not just fields, since the
    four methods only ever touched their own three fields plus the
    _maxClipboardCaptureLength bound and the free _resolveITerm2ClipboardSelector()
    helper - a fully self-contained unit.
    
    Terminal's startITerm2ClipboardCapture/endITerm2ClipboardCapture
    EscapeHandler overrides, and the internal
    _captureITerm2ClipboardChar/_captureITerm2ClipboardTextRange helpers,
    now thin-delegate to _clipboardCapture; endITerm2ClipboardCapture's
    "selector==null || buffer==null || overflowed => don't store" branch
    moves into _ClipboardCapture.end(), which returns null in exactly
    those cases so the call site is unchanged behaviorally. reset() and
    dispose() now call _clipboardCapture.reset() instead of clearing the
    three fields by hand.
    
    terminal.dart drops from 4440 to 4401 lines; terminal_clipboard.dart
    adds 78.
    
