[33mcommit 4cc21c542a63c72a1ce5784f8c7dc22a01638000[m
Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 23:26:16 2026 +0300

    refactor(terminal): extract mode flags into _TerminalModes
    
    Terminal.reset() and Terminal.softReset() each hand-reset ~35 mode
    fields and duplicated roughly 80% of each other, so adding a new mode
    meant editing the field declaration, reset(), and softReset() as three
    separate, uncoordinated sites.
    
    Move every DEC/ANSI mode flag (insert, origin, autowrap, mouse
    tracking, kitty keyboard stack, synchronized-update, etc.) into a new
    _TerminalModes class with its own reset()/softReset() methods, and
    have Terminal.reset()/softReset() delegate to it. The two methods
    intentionally still differ: full reset() also clears
    _cursorLineHighlightMode, which softReset() (DECSTR) does not touch -
    that asymmetry is preserved exactly.
    
    _TerminalModes lives in terminal_modes.dart as `part of 'terminal.dart'`
    so it shares the library with Terminal and needs no import boundary
    for the many private fields it holds; the leading underscore keeps it
    out of the public API entirely (core.dart only exports
    'src/terminal.dart', and part-file declarations follow the same
    export rules as the primary file).
    
    No behavior change: field defaults, and the reset()/softReset() field
    sets, are copied verbatim. terminal.dart drops from 4594 to 4453
    lines; terminal_modes.dart adds 174.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

