    feat(escape): add opt-in onUnknownSequence diagnostic callback
    
    Developers integrating xterm2 have no way to answer "why isn't my
    escape sequence working?" since unrecognised ESC/CSI/OSC/DCS input is
    silently (and correctly) ignored. Add Terminal.onUnknownSequence to
    observe those drops without changing what the terminal does with them.
    
    Hooked into the three existing unknownEscape/unknownCSI dispatch
    points, the OSC fallback dispatch (excluding OSC 133/633/3008, which
    share that fallback but are actually handled), and a new
    EscapeHandler.unknownDCS for DCS payloads that match no known request.
    
    The callback is null-guarded before any string work happens, so it
    costs nothing on the hot path when unset. When set, the raw sequence
    is reconstructed from the parser's byte consumer and formatted with
    the same convention TerminalDebugger already uses for readability.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

