Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 21:24:13 2026 +0300

    fix(buffer): clear stale wide-char lead exposed by growing a resized line
    
    Fuzzing (test/src/core/escape/parser_fuzz_test.dart, seed 0xdeadbeef)
    found two bugs that share one root cause:
    
    - round 506: a width-2 cell can end up in the very last column of a
      line with no room left for its width-0 placeholder cell, breaking the
      wide-char/placeholder pairing invariant.
    - round 2827: Buffer.resize -> reflow() -> _LineReflow._addPart ->
      BufferLine.getWidth later crashes with `RangeError: ... -1`, reading
      one column past where it expects a placeholder to exist.
    
    Root cause: BufferLine.resize() intentionally preserves cell data
    beyond the new logical length when a line shrinks (this is relied on
    elsewhere - see the "preserves hidden cells"/"preserves hidden combining
    characters" tests - so a line grown back later can recover its old
    content). But when a previously-shrunk line is grown again, the newly
    exposed cell at the new last column can be a stale width-2 lead left
    over from an even earlier, larger width, whose paired placeholder cell
    is still outside the new (smaller-than-that-original-width) length.
    `reflow()`'s final resize pass (and Buffer.resize's non-reflow
    fallback path) called `line.resize(newWidth)` directly with no check
    for this, unlike `_LineReflow.add()` which already guards its own
    resize calls the same way. That dangling lead is exactly the corrupt
    state bug 2827's reflow pass chokes on and computes a negative index
    for.
    
    Fix: after growing a line to `newWidth` in both of these call sites,
    clear the cell at `newWidth - 1` if it turns out to be a stale wide
    lead with no room for its placeholder - the same guard `_LineReflow.add`
    already applies. This single fix closes both regressions (2827 no
    longer reproduces once 506's corruption can no longer occur), so both
    tests are un-skipped here.
    
    While verifying with XTERM2_FUZZ_ROUNDS=5000, a third, unrelated
    wide-char corruption surfaced (seed 0xc0ffee, round 3225, triggered by
    a lone ESC ESC token, no resize involved). It reproduces identically
    before this fix, so it is not a regression introduced here. Recorded
    as a new skipped regression test rather than fixed, since it has a
    different root cause and is out of scope for this change.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

