Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 19:43:37 2026 +0300

    test(parser): add seeded fuzz harness with invariant checks
    
    There is no fuzzing today for EscapeParser (~3077 lines of state
    transitions in lib/src/core/escape/parser.dart), covered only by
    hand-written scenarios. Add a fuzz harness that drives the parser
    through Terminal.write (so Terminal's own EscapeHandler wiring is
    exercised end to end) with a mix of plain/wide/combining text, CSI
    sequences with random prefixes/params/finals, terminated and
    unterminated OSC (including embedded lone ESC), DCS with oversized
    payloads, lone ESC / ESC+C0 / ESC+ESC, CAN/SUB interrupting in-flight
    sequences, and truncated sequences split across multiple write() calls
    to exercise the parser's rollback/resume path.
    
    Move the invariant helper from the stress test into a shared
    test/_support/terminal_invariants.dart so both suites reuse the same
    checks. Iterate over a fixed list of seeds for deterministic CI, with
    XTERM2_FUZZ_ROUNDS available for a longer local run.
    
    The harness found two real bugs in lib/ (not fixed here, per scope):
    a width-2 cell can land in a line's last column with no room for its
    placeholder cell (seed 0xdeadbeef, round 506), and Buffer.resize's
    reflow throws a RangeError afterwards (same seed, round 2827). Both
    are filed as skip-ped regression tests with raw (unminimized but
    reliable) repros.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

