Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 19:35:30 2026 +0300

    perf(render): replace O(n log n) paragraph cache eviction with O(1) LRU
    
    maximumSize defaults to 2048 with an eviction batch of maximumSize >> 4
    (128), so every 128 newly cached glyphs the previous implementation
    copied all 2048 map entries into a List and sorted it just to find the
    least-recently-used ones.
    
    Replace that with a binary min-heap of (lastUsed, key) snapshots ordered
    by recency. Eviction pops the smallest entries in O(log n) each instead
    of resorting the whole cache. getLayoutFromCache() (the hit path) is left
    completely untouched - it still only bumps entry.lastUsed and never
    touches the heap or the map, preserving that intentional optimization.
    
    Because hits don't update the heap, a heap node's recorded lastUsed can
    go stale relative to the entry's current lastUsed. This is handled with
    lazy repair: when eviction pops a node whose recorded lastUsed doesn't
    match the entry's current lastUsed, the node is stale (the entry was hit,
    or replaced, since the node was pushed), so it's re-pushed with the
    up-to-date value and the search continues. This is a standard
    lazy-deletion/decrease-key pattern for heaps and keeps eviction correct
    without ever mutating the heap on a cache hit.
    
    .dispose() is still called on every evicted paragraph, and clear()/
    dispose() semantics (drop and dispose everything, including now the
    heap) are unchanged. painter.dart's paragraphCacheLength getter still
    reads _cache.length and is unaffected.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

