Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 19:34:25 2026 +0300

    fix(terminal): prune hyperlink URIs when scrollback lines are evicted
    
    Previously _pruneUnusedHyperlinks() only ran when the registry hit its
    4096-entry ceiling, so hyperlinks tied to lines long gone from scrollback
    lingered until then and were reclaimed by one bulk O(n) scan.
    
    Add an optional onEvict callback to IndexAwareCircularBuffer, invoked in
    push() right after a line is trimmed off the front due to overflow. Terminal
    wires this up on both buffers: when a line is evicted, it collects the
    hyperlink ids that lived on that line and checks only those ids for whether
    they're still referenced elsewhere (cursor style or any live cell in either
    buffer), removing them - and their _explicitHyperlinkIds entries - if not.
    This keeps the registry roughly bounded by live hyperlinks instead of
    growing toward the ceiling, without adding any cost to the per-cell write
    path.
    
    Adds a @visibleForTesting Terminal.debugHyperlinkCount accessor since there
    is no other public way to observe registry size, used by a new test that
    writes hyperlinks past scrollback capacity and asserts the registry stays
    bounded.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

