Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Sun Aug 2 16:18:19 2026 +0300

    fix(input): commit composing text before dispatching an IME action
    
    On Android, Gboard and the Samsung keyboard keep a typed word in the
    composing region until it is committed. `updateEditingValue` returns
    early while a composing range is active, so nothing reaches the
    terminal; `performAction` meanwhile dispatched the action immediately.
    Pressing enter after typing `htop` therefore emitted `\rhtop` instead of
    `htop\r` - the newline overtook the text it was meant to follow, and the
    command never ran.
    
    `performAction` now flushes any active composing range first, so the
    text is inserted before the action is dispatched. Android often follows
    up by sending that same text again as a collapsed editing value, so the
    committed text is remembered and the duplicate is dropped. When an IME
    batches a further edit onto its final commit, only the portion beyond
    the already-committed text is inserted, which keeps that character from
    being lost.
    
    Ported from a downstream patch that had been carried against 5.2.0 in a
    vendored copy; the two tests come with it. Both fail on the unpatched
    tree with exactly the reported `'\rhtop'` output.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

