Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Sun Aug 2 15:06:49 2026 +0300

    perf(rendering): avoid map mutation on paragraph cache hits
    
    `getLayoutFromCache` implemented LRU recency by removing the entry and
    re-inserting it, so every cache *hit* mutated the underlying map. The
    painter looks up one cached paragraph per visible cell per frame, which
    made this two hash operations plus a reinsertion for every glyph on
    screen: measured at 926 lookups per frame for a typical 80x24 shell
    screen, so roughly 1850 map mutations per frame spent purely on reads.
    
    Entries now carry a `lastUsed` stamp taken from a monotonic counter.
    Reads bump that field instead of touching the map at all. Recency
    ordering is preserved, but it is now resolved at eviction time by
    scanning for the oldest entries rather than being maintained on every
    read.
    
    Eviction drops a batch (1/16 of the cache, at least one entry) in a
    single pass so the linear scan is amortized to O(1) per insertion
    instead of running on every overflow.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

